osures of\n$T_1$ and $T_2$ are disjoint."], "original_pass2_hypotheses_proposed": ["Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme.\nLet $U \\subset X$ be a quasi-compact open.", "If $Z_1, Z_2 \\subset X$ are closed subschemes of finite\npresentation such that $Z_1 \\cap Z_2 \\cap U = \\emptyset$,", "If $T_1, T_2 \\subset U$ are disjoint constructible closed subsets,"], "original_source_statement_tex": "\\label{lemma-separate-disjoint-locally-closed-by-blowing-up}\nLet $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme.\nLet $U \\subset X$ be a quasi-compact open.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item If $Z_1, Z_2 \\subset X$ are closed subschemes of finite\npresentation such that $Z_1 \\cap Z_2 \\cap U = \\emptyset$, then\nthere exists a $U$-admissible blowing up $X' \\to X$\nsuch that the strict transforms of $Z_1$ and $Z_2$ are disjoint.\n\\item If $T_1, T_2 \\subset U$ are disjoint constructible closed subsets, then\nthere is a $U$-admissible blowing up $X' \\to X$ such that the closures of\n$T_1$ and $T_2$ are disjoint.\n\\end{enumerate}", "pass3_eligible": false, "published": false, "schema": "maththm.four-complete-chapters.standalone-editorial-draft.v1", "section_ambient_hypotheses_auto_inherited": [], "section_end_line": 10001, "section_index": 194, "section_key": "s194", "section_start_line": 9532, "section_title": "Nagata compactification", "source_enumerated_clauses": ["If $Z_1, Z_2 \\subset X$ are closed subschemes of finite\npresentation such that $Z_1 \\cap Z_2 \\cap U = \\emptyset$, then\nthere exists a $U$-admissible blowing up $X' \\to X$\nsuch that the strict transforms of $Z_1$ and $Z_2$ are disjoint.", "If $T_1, T_2 \\subset U$ are disjoint constructible closed subsets, then\nthere is a $U$-admissible blowing up $X' \\to X$ such that the closures of\n$T_1$ and $T_2$ are disjoint."], "source_filename": "flat.tex", "source_formal_environment": "lemma", "source_formal_environment_end_line": 9566, "source_formal_environment_start_line": 9553, "source_inline_reference_labels": [], "source_label": "lemma-separate-disjoint-locally-closed-by-blowing-up", "source_logical_form": "listed_assertions_with_individual_guards", "source_named_reference_labels": [], "source_proof_screened": false, "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scoped_conventions_and_situations": [], "source_statement_line": 9553, "source_url": "https://github.com/stacks/stacks-project/blob/a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14/flat.tex#L9553", "standalone_statement_tex": "Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme.\nLet $U \\subset X$ be a quasi-compact open.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item If $Z_1, Z_2 \\subset X$ are closed subschemes of finite\npresentation such that $Z_1 \\cap Z_2 \\cap U = \\emptyset$, then\nthere exists a $U$-admissible blowing up $X' \\to X$\nsuch that the strict transforms of $Z_1$ and $Z_2$ are disjoint.\n\\item If $T_1, T_2 \\subset U$ are disjoint constructible closed subsets, then\nthere is a $U$-admissible blowing up $X' \\to X$ such that the closures of\n$T_1$ and $T_2$ are disjoint.\n\\end{enumerate}"}
